{
  "_about": "HDLC framing as RICSerial uses it. Made from RaftCore MiniHDLC by linux_unit_tests/test_comms_framing_vectors --write - do not edit. Frame: flag, escaped(payload, CRC high, CRC low), flag. Bytes equal to the flag or escape are sent as escape, byte ^ 0x20. CRC is CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE (poly 0x1021, init 0xffff) of the payload. Decoding: bytes from one flag to the next are a frame if there are at least 2 and the last 2 are the CRC of the others (bytes before the first flag count as a frame too); otherwise they are dropped. A frame longer than maxLen (payload + CRC) is discarded at that point and decoding starts again from the next byte.",
